<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">27 September in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 27 September, from 1331 to 1964.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/teutonic-order.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1331">1331 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">695 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Teutonic Order defeats the Poles at the Battle of Płowce</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At Płowce, forces of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-poland">Kingdom of Poland</a> fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a>; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poles">Poles</a> were defeated, but their leaders escaped capture.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1422">1422 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">604 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Treaty of Melno fixes the Prussian–Lithuanian border</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Signed near Lake Melno by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Knights</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-poland">Kingdom of Poland</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-duchy-of-lithuania">Grand Duchy of Lithuania</a>, the treaty ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gollub-war">Gollub War</a>. The Order gave up its claims to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samogitia">Samogitia</a>, and the border it fixed lasted about five centuries.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-melno">Treaty of Melno</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1529">1529 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">497 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Suleiman the Magnificent begins the siege of Vienna</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suleiman-the-magnificent">Suleiman the Magnificent</a> attacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a> with over 100,000 men in the first Ottoman attempt to take the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> capital, defended by no more than 21,000 under Niklas Graf Salm. The city held out until the siege ended on 15 October.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siege-of-vienna-1529">Siege of Vienna (1529)</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1540">1540 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">486 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pope Paul III approves the Society of Jesus</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The bull Regimini militantis Ecclesiae formally established <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ignatius-of-loyola">Ignatius of Loyola</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuits</a>. The order became a leading force of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/counter-reformation">Catholic Reformation</a>, founding schools and missions worldwide.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuits</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1669">1669 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">357 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Venice surrenders Candia to the Ottomans</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Venetians handed over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heraklion">Candia</a>, modern Heraklion, ending a siege of more than 21 years, one of the longest in history. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crete">Crete</a> passed to Ottoman rule.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crete">Crete</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1825">1825 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">201 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Stockton and Darlington Railway opens</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">George Stephenson drove Locomotion No. 1, hauling <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coal">coal</a> wagons and hundreds of passengers, on the opening run. It was the world's first public railway to use <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/steam-locomotive">steam locomotives</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1940">1940 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">86 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Germany, Italy and Japan sign the Tripartite Pact</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The three powers signed a ten-year military alliance in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a>, pledging mutual aid if attacked by a power not yet at war, aimed chiefly at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>. It formalised the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/axis-powers">Axis</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1964">1964 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">62 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Warren Commission report is made public</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The commission's report concluded that Lee Harvey Oswald alone had killed President Kennedy. Its findings have been widely debated ever since.</p></div></li></ol>
